{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>On the day of the new month, etc.</b> This erection took place after the seven days of consecration, according to their words, of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah ch. 13), and so the verses prove, for during the seven days of consecration nothing was done except the consecration of Aaron's hands. Therefore HaShem commanded the act of the seven days of consecration before the commandment to erect the Tabernacle and arrange it. And also in parashat Tzav, when He anointed Aaron and his sons on the first day of consecration, there He mentioned the anointing of the Tabernacle and its vessels, but He did not mention there the erection of the Tabernacle and its arrangement. From this you learn that the consecrations preceded the erection of the Tabernacle and the arrangement of its vessels, and the day of the new moon of Nisan is when the Tabernacle was sanctified, and Moses arranged the setup of the Tabernacle and offered in it what is stated concerning the matter. From this you learn that Moses did not serve in the Tabernacle in the order of everything stated in this parashah except on a single day, which is the eighth day of consecration. And even according to those who hold that during all seven days of consecration Moses would build the Tabernacle and dismantle it (Jerusalemite Yoma 1:5), it is necessarily the case to say that the Tabernacle is what he would build and dismantle, but the arrangement of its setup was only on the day of the new moon of Nisan, as stated concerning the matter: ״On the first day of the month, etc. and you shall set there, etc. and you shall bring the table,״ etc. See — it is from the new month that He informs him of the arrangement and the place of each thing and the order of its placement; and if this were already for seven days and he was arranging them, what room would there be to inform him anew from the new month? Rather, certainly this day is the beginning of the order of the Tabernacle's construction and its setup, and Moses offered in it on that day everything stated concerning the matter, by HaShem's command to him, as stated before us."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:24.402711805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}